Solar and wind are inexhaustible on any human timescale — the sun delivers 10,000 times more energy to Earth's surface each day than humanity consumes.
Denmark regularly generates over 100% of its electricity needs from wind; Portugal ran on 100% renewables for 6 consecutive days in 2023.
Battery storage costs have fallen 97% since 1991, enabling grids to store excess renewable generation for calm or cloudy periods.
The IEA projects that renewables will account for 90% of global electricity capacity additions through 2026 — this is already happening at scale.
